## 3. k-d Tree (O(log n) — Practical General Solution)

For the general case, k-d trees give O(log n) average query time. Degrades to O(n) in high dimensions (curse of dimensionality).

**Build:** O(n log n)  
**Query:** O(log n) average, O(n) worst case  
**Space:** O(n)

## 4. LSH (Approximate, Sublinear)

If you can tolerate approximation, Locality-Sensitive Hashing gives sublinear query time even in high dimensions.

